        <!-- Q-Legal -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">What is the legal difference between a private driver and an official city tour guide in Morocco?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              Under Moroccan tourism regulations (Law 05-12 enforced by the Ministry of Tourism), there is a strict legal distinction between a private tourist chauffeur (<em>Transport Touristique</em>) and a licensed municipal tour guide (<em>guide des villes et circuits</em>). A private driver is licensed to navigate national highways, mountain passes, airport corridors, manage luggage, translate Darija and Berber, recommend authentic culinary stops, and share cultural context during road travel.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px;">
              However, by law, private chauffeurs cannot conduct guided historical tours inside enclosed heritage monuments and medinas (such as Bahia Palace, Medersa Ben Youssef, Volubilis, or the Fes Tanneries). For enclosed historical landmarks, Roam Morocco seamlessly arranges licensed, badge-holding municipal guides on demand to ensure full legal compliance and an enriching historical experience without street tout interference.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q-Licensing -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">Why is hiring an officially licensed Transport Touristique vehicle critical over an unlicensed taxi?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              Official tourist transport vehicles in Morocco operate under a strict Ministry of Tourism permit (<em>Agrément de Transport Touristique</em>), recognizable by green or blue commercial plates, comprehensive commercial passenger insurance (<em>Assurance Transport</em>), and an official mission manifest (<em>Ordre de Mission</em>). Royal Gendarmerie and Sûreté Nationale highway checkpoints strictly inspect these credentials on all routes.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px;">
              Unlicensed private cars or informal pirate taxis recruited off street corners or social media lack commercial passenger liability insurance and face immediate vehicle impoundment at police checkpoints, stranding travelers on rural mountain roads. Roam Morocco operates 100% legally compliant, accredited vehicles with full passenger liability protection.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q-SoloFemale -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">Is it safe for solo female travelers to hire a private driver in Morocco?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              <strong>Yes, absolutely.</strong> Roam Morocco is deeply trusted by solo female travelers from around the world. All our chauffeurs are vetted, experienced Berber and Moroccan hospitality professionals with clean criminal background records.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px;">
              Your chauffeur acts as your dedicated local guardian—meeting you inside airport arrivals, escorting you on foot directly to your riad's inner doorway at night so you never walk through unfamiliar medina alleys alone, shielding you from aggressive market touts, and maintaining respectful professional boundaries throughout your trip.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q-MotionSickness -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">How do your drivers handle mountain roads and motion sickness over the High Atlas Tizi n'Tichka pass?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              Crossing the High Atlas via the 2,260-meter Tizi n'Tichka pass requires seasoned mountain driving skill. Our chauffeurs have decades of experience navigating these mountain curves with gentle acceleration, smooth engine braking, and a calm, unhurried pace. We schedule frequent scenic photo pauses at panoramic viewpoints, carry fresh bottled water and complimentary natural ginger candies/remedies, and tailor driving speed immediately to passenger comfort.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q-FlightDelay -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">What happens if our flight into Casablanca or Marrakech airport is delayed?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              All Roam Morocco airport pickups include complimentary live flight radar tracking. Whether your flight into Casablanca Mohammed V (CMN) or Marrakech Menara (RAK) lands early or is delayed by several hours, your chauffeur tracks your actual arrival time and will be waiting curbside at the terminal with a personalized name board at no additional charge.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q3 -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">What languages do your private drivers speak?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              All our private chauffeurs are fluent in <strong>English, French, and Moroccan Arabic (Darija)</strong>, with many also speaking Berber dialects. They are seasoned hospitality professionals who can translate at local markets, explain cultural customs, and ensure you always feel understood and respected.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q4 -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">Can we stop for photos, coffee, or scenic vistas whenever we want?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              <strong>Always.</strong> Unlike rigid tour buses, a private driver operates entirely around your rhythm. If you spot a panoramic view of the snow-capped High Atlas, want to stretch your legs at a roadside date stand, or wish to sleep in an extra hour before departing, your chauffeur is at your complete disposal.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q5 -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">How does luggage and riad dropoff work in pedestrian-only medinas?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              In historical medinas such as Marrakech, Fes, and Chefchaouen, cars cannot enter the narrow medieval alleyways. Your driver pulls up to the closest secure gate (Bab). Before arrival, your driver contacts your riad manager on WhatsApp so riad staff or licensed porters meet you curbside with handcarts to escort you directly to check-in.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q6 -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">What is the customary tip for a private driver in Morocco?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              Tipping is customary and greatly appreciated for professional service. A standard gratuity is <strong>100 to 150 MAD (€10 to €15) per day</strong> from a couple, or <strong>200 to 300 MAD (€20 to €30) per day</strong> for a family or small group. Tips are typically given directly to your chauffeur in cash on the final day of your journey.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q7 -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">Do you provide child safety car seats?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              Yes. We provide sanitized, European-certified infant capsules, forward-facing child seats, and booster seats <strong>free of charge</strong> upon request. Simply let us know the ages and approximate weights of your children when requesting your quote.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q8 -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">How far in advance should I reserve a private driver?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              For peak travel seasons (March through May, September through November, and Christmas/New Year), we recommend booking <strong>6 to 12 weeks in advance</strong> to guarantee top-tier English-speaking drivers and modern Prado 4x4s. For low season travel (July, August, January), 2 to 3 weeks notice is generally sufficient.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q-MedinaRiad -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">How does riad pickup and luggage handling work in pedestrian medinas like Fes and Marrakech?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              Because ancient medinas like Fes el-Bali and Marrakech Medina are completely pedestrianized, vehicles cannot drive through the narrow residential alleyways. Your Roam Morocco chauffeur parks securely at the closest vehicle gate (Bab) and walks directly to your riad reception desk at the agreed time to greet you in person.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px;">
              For your luggage, your driver liaises directly with your riad manager in advance or coordinates licensed medina handcart porters (<em>charettes</em>) to escort all suitcases between your riad doorway and the vehicle. You never have to search for a car or haul heavy bags across cobblestones.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q-DirectTransfers -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">Can I book direct private airport transfers from Casablanca (CMN) to Fes or Marrakech without booking a full tour?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              <strong>Yes, absolutely.</strong> Private intercity airport transfers are one of our core daily services. We provide direct VIP transfers connecting Casablanca Mohammed V Airport (CMN) with Fes (&euro;170 flat rate), Casablanca Airport with Marrakech (&euro;130–&euro;140 flat rate), and transfers from Marrakech Menara (RAK) or Fes-Sa&iuml;ss (FEZ).
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px;">
              Every airport transfer includes 24/7 flight radar tracking, meet-and-greet inside arrivals with a personalized name board, baggage assistance, all highway tolls, and door-to-door medina riad gate coordination.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q-FleetGuarantee -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">Are vehicles guaranteed to be the exact model booked (such as Toyota Prado 4x4 or Mercedes V-Class)?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              <strong>Yes, 100%.</strong> Roam Morocco operates a strict "No Bait-and-Switch" fleet guarantee. When you reserve a Toyota Land Cruiser Prado TXL 4x4 or a Mercedes-Benz V-Class VIP, that is the exact model dispatched for your journey. Every vehicle is a recent model (2022–2025), equipped with automatic transmission, high-output air conditioning, commercial passenger transport licensing (<em>Transport Touristique S&eacute;rie T</em>), and full passenger insurance.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q-CustomStops -->
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h4 class="faq-question">Can we customize en-route stops (such as wineries, argan oil cooperatives, or photography viewpoints) on day trips?</h4>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>
              <strong>Yes, always.</strong> Private travel with Roam Morocco is completely flexible and tailored to your rhythm. On journeys such as Marrakech to Essaouira, you can pause at organic wineries (such as <em>Le Domaine du Val d’Argan</em> in Ounagha) for tastings and lunch, visit authentic women's argan oil cooperatives, or stop at scenic olive orchards. Your chauffeur waits for you at each destination at zero extra charge.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

